---
import "../styles/legal.css";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Nav from "../components/Nav.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import { company, seo } from "../content/site";

const updated = "September 29, 2026";
---

<Base title={seo.privacy.title} description={seo.privacy.description} path="/privacy">
  <Nav />
  <main class="legal">
    <div class="aurora"></div>
    <div class="wrap">
      <article class="glass legal-card reveal">
        <span class="label">Legal</span>
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="legal-meta">Last updated {updated} · {company.legalName} ({company.brand})</p>

        <p>
          This Privacy Policy explains how {company.legalName} (“River,” “we,” “us”) collects, uses, and
          shares information when you visit riverph.com, use Smart Refill, River for Business, River Mobile,
          or related products for water refilling stations, laundry shops, carwashes, and other local
          service businesses in the {company.country}. River Tech was founded in {company.foundedYear} together
          with the Smart Refill app.
        </p>
        <p>
          This is a starter policy for our marketing site and product ecosystem. Product-specific notices
          may apply inside signed-in workspaces and apps. If anything here conflicts with an in-product
          notice for a paid or authenticated service, that notice controls for that service.
        </p>

        <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          {company.legalName} builds AI-powered operations tools for neighborhood businesses and River Mobile,
          the household app that connects customers to their local providers. Founded in {company.foundedYear}
          with Smart Refill, our principal place of business is {company.officeAddress}. Contact:{" "}
          <a href={`mailto:${company.contactEmail}`}>{company.contactEmail}</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>2. Information we collect</h2>
        <p>Depending on how you interact with River, we may collect:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Contact and inquiry data</strong> — name, business type, city, and mobile number when you
            submit a partner interest form or email us.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Account and business data</strong> — workspace profile, staff roles, order/delivery records,
            inventory, rider activity, water-quality/TDS updates, and similar operations data inside Smart Refill
            and River for Business.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Customer app data</strong> — River Mobile account details, provider preferences, order history,
            QR scan events, delivery tracking events, and device notifications you enable.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Technical data</strong> — IP address, browser type, device identifiers, pages viewed, and
            approximate location derived from network data when you browse our marketing site.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>3. How we use information</h2>
        <p>We use information to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Operate, secure, and improve River products and the marketing site</li>
          <li>Respond to partner inquiries and provide onboarding support</li>
          <li>Process orders, deliveries, inventory alerts, and customer communications for partner businesses</li>
          <li>Power AI features such as dashboards, forecasting, scanning helpers, and insights from a shop’s own data</li>
          <li>Send service notices; marketing messages only where permitted and with a clear way to opt out</li>
          <li>Comply with law and protect the rights and safety of users, partners, and River</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>4. AI features</h2>
        <p>
          Some River products include AI-assisted summaries, forecasts, and insights. These features are designed
          to help owners run water stations, laundry shops, carwashes, and similar businesses more efficiently.
          We use business and operational data you provide in-product to generate those outputs. We do not sell
          your customer lists as a standalone product.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Sharing</h2>
        <p>We may share information with:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Service providers who host infrastructure, analytics, messaging, or support tools under contract</li>
          <li>Partner businesses and their staff when you are their customer using River Mobile</li>
          <li>Riders or fulfillment staff assigned to complete a delivery or service request</li>
          <li>Authorities when required by law or to protect against fraud, abuse, or security incidents</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We do not sell personal information for money.</p>

        <h2>6. Retention</h2>
        <p>
          We keep information only as long as needed for the purposes above, including legal, accounting, and
          dispute-resolution requirements. Marketing-site inquiry data is retained while we evaluate partnership
          interest and for a reasonable follow-up period unless you ask us to delete it sooner where applicable.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Security</h2>
        <p>
          We use administrative, technical, and organizational measures appropriate to the sensitivity of the
          data we handle. No method of transmission or storage is perfectly secure; please use strong credentials
          and tell us promptly about suspected unauthorized access.
        </p>

        <h2>8. Your choices</h2>
        <p>
          Depending on your relationship with River and applicable Philippine law, you may request access,
          correction, or deletion of personal information we hold, or ask questions about this policy, by
          emailing <a href={`mailto:${company.contactEmail}`}>{company.contactEmail}</a>. River Mobile users can
          also manage notification preferences in the app when available.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Children</h2>
        <p>
          River products are directed to businesses and adult household users. We do not knowingly collect
          personal information from children for marketing or account creation.
        </p>

        <h2>10. Changes</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. The “Last updated” date at the top will change
          when we do. Continued use of the site or products after an update means you acknowledge the revised
          policy.
        </p>

        <h2>11. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          {company.legalName}<br />
          {company.officeAddress}<br />
          <a href={`mailto:${company.contactEmail}`}>{company.contactEmail}</a>
        </p>

        <a class="legal-back" href="/">← Back to River Apps</a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>
